This data visualization project analyzes the global automotive market to understand the relationships between various vehicle characteristics, origins, pricing, and sales performance. The researchers merged, cleaned, and pre-processed two datasets, utilizing Python libraries such as Pandas and Plotly to generate a series of interactive graphs, including Map Plots (Scattergeo), Scatter Plots, and Bar Charts. Key insights from the visual analysis reveal that the United States dominates in car manufacturing volume, while technical comparisons demonstrate a direct correlation between a car's weight and its horsepower, as well as an inverse relationship between fuel capacity and fuel efficiency.
